            <ArticleTitle>Laparoscopic incidental appendectomy.</ArticleTitle>
            <Pagination>
                <MedlinePgn>116-8</MedlinePgn>
            </Pagination>
            <Abstract>
                <AbstractText>The benefits and risks of laparoscopic incidental appendectomy are discussed. We believe a case for laparoscopic incidental appendectomy can be made for patients undergoing diagnostic laparoscopy for lower abdominal pain in whom either no cause is found, or in whom a cause other than appendicitis is discovered. No benefit from incidental appendectomy can be shown for patients undergoing laparoscopy for other disorders.</AbstractText>
            </Abstract>
